# Copy to .vocabulary-denylist (gitignored) and add literal terms that must
# never be committed to this public repository.
#
# One term per line. Case-insensitive substring match. Lines starting with #
# are ignored.
#
# This .example file is committed; the real .vocabulary-denylist is NOT.
# That split is deliberate — a committed list of internal codenames would
# publish the very names it is meant to protect.
#
# In CI, supply the same content as the VOCABULARY_DENYLIST repository secret.
#
# Examples of the KINDS of things to list (do not commit real values):
#   <your-internal-sso-system-name>
#   <your-internal-wiki-hostname>
#   <your-company-name-if-unannounced>
#   <internal-project-codename>
